## Question 15

A 65-year-old male presents to the ED with complaints of frequent urination, especially at night, difficulty initiating urination, and a sensation of incomplete bladder emptying. On physical examination, his prostate is enlarged, smooth, and non-tender. He is diagnosed with benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH). Which of the following medications can help alleviate bladder spasms and provide symptom relief in this patient?

