## Question 3

Transverse thoracic plane lies at the level of which of the following anatomically relations?

- A. 4th intercostal space
- B. 3rd intercostal space
- **C. 2nd intercostal space** (Correct Answer)
- D. 5th intercostal space
- E. 1st intercostal space

**Correct Answer:** C

**Explanation:**

Transverse thoracic plane lies at the level of 2nd intercostal space and intervertebral disc between T4 & T5

CLAPTRAP is useful mnemonic to remember structures transected by transverse thoracic plane.

C: cardiac plexus L: ligamentum arteriosum A: aortic arch (inner concavity) RECALL P: pulmonary trunk bifurcation T: tracheal bifurcation (carina) RECALL R: right-to-left movement of the thoracic duct (posterior to the esophagus)

A: azygos vein drains into superior vena cava P: pre-vertebral fascia and pre-tracheal fascia end

