Left coronary artery gives rise to two branches

The anterior interventricular branch: supply the right and left ventricle, the apex and anterior two third of interventricular septum.

Left circumflex branch: supplying the left atrium and left ventricle

The right coronary artery supplies:

the right atrium and most of right ventricle the sinoatrial and atrioventricular node

