## Question 2

The phrenic nerve receive contributions from which of the following?

- A. Anterior rami of C1 -C3
- B. Anterior rami to C4 -C7
- **C. Anterior rami of C3 - C5** (Correct Answer)
- D. Posterior rami of C1 -C3
- E. Posterior rami of C3 -C5

**Correct Answer:** C

**Explanation:**

The phrenic nerve originates from cervical spinal roots C3, C4 and C5 provide motor innervation to the diaphragm (RECALL).

provide sensory innervation the central part of the diaphragm, the pericardium and the mediastinal part of the parietal pleura. (RECALL)

