## Question 8

You have been asked to make a Quick assessment of patient's upper limb neurology as a part of secondary survey. You test each dermatome and note the patient has no sensation at the medial antecubital fossa. The medial antecubital fossa tests which of the following dermatomes?

- A. C6
- B. C8
- C. C7
- **D. T1** (Correct Answer)
- E. C5

**Correct Answer:** D

**Explanation:**

DERMATOMES C2= occipital protuberance (RECALL) C3= supraclavicular fossa C4= Acromioclavicular joint (RECALL) C5 = lateral antecubital fossa C6= thumb (RECALL)

C7=middle finger C8=little finger T1= medial antecubital fossa T2= Apex of axilla

