> | Inferomedial border | Medial head of gastrocnemius (Recall) |
> | Inferolateral border | Lateral head of gastrocnemius and plantaris |
> |  | The floor of the popliteal fossa is formed by the posterior surface of the knee |
> | Floor | joint capsule, popliteus muscle and posterior femur. |
> |  | The roof is made of up two layers: popliteal fascia and skin. The popliteal |
> | Roof | fascia is continuous with the deep fascia of the leg. |
> | Contents | Popliteal artery, popliteal vein, tibial nerve, common fibular nerve |

- **A. Weakness of plantarflexion and inversion** (Correct Answer)
- B. Weakness of dorsiflexion and eversion
- C. Foot drop
- D. Loss of flexion of the leg at the knee joint
- E. Loss of extension of the leg at the knee joint

**Correct Answer:** A

**Explanation:**

Tibial and common fibular nerve are the most superficial contents of the popliteal fossa. Both are the branches of sciatic nerve

The common fibular nerve follows the biceps femoris tendon, travelling along the lateral margin of the popliteal Tibial nerve lies more medial

