**Explanation:**

loop diuretic e.g.: furosemide inhibit the Na+k+2C L- symporter on luminal membrane in the thick ascending limb of loop of Henle thus preventing t he reabsorption of Nacl and water while thiazides act mainly on early segment of distal tubule where they inhibit the Nacl reabsorption by binding to the Na+cl- cotransporter (RECALL).

