## Question 15

you are prescribing ipratropium bromide for a patient who has presented with an exacerbation of her COPD. what is mechanism of action of ipratropium bromide?

> *Image in the question (OCR text, if any)*
> *(no readable text in the image)*

- A. Beta agonist
- **B. Muscarinic antagonist** (Correct Answer)
- C. Ca channel blocker
- D. Muscarinic agonist
- E. Alpha agonist

**Correct Answer:** B

**Explanation:**

Ipratropium is an acetylcholine antagonist via blockade of muscarinic cholinergic receptors. Blocking cholinergic receptors decreases the production of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGM P). This decrease in the lung airways will lead to decreased contraction of the smooth muscles.

**Answer key, Quiz 15:** 1-B, 2-D, 3-C, 4-C, 5-D, 6-A, 7-A, 8-E, 9-D, 10-B, 11-E, 12-C, 13-A, 14-E, 15-B


