## Question 6

Regarding the power of study which one of the following statements is correct?

- A. Power does not change with sample size
- **B. Power increases with sample size** (Correct Answer)
- C. Power increases as the variability increases
- D. Power decreases with sample size
- E. Power decreases as the variability decrease

**Correct Answer:** B

**Explanation:**

The power of a study is the probability of (correctly) rejecting the null hypothesis when it is false, i. e. the probability of detecting a statistically significant difference

power can be increased by increasing the sample size Power increases as the variability decrease

Note: Increasing sample size can decrease bias /error. (Recall)

