## Question 15

A 5-year-old school-going child gets exposed to measles. What should parents be advised about returning to school?

> *Image in the question (OCR text, if any)*
> *(no readable text in the image)*

- A. 5 days from onset of rash
- B. After 24 hours of fever
- C. 6 days after rash has gone
- D. When all lesions are crusted over
- **E. 4 days from onset of rash** (Correct Answer)

**Correct Answer:** E

**Explanation:**

Patients are considered infectious for 3 days before the rash emerges and are advised to stay away from school or for four days from onset of the rash.

Note: Regarding rubella: Patients are infectious from 7 days before the rash appears and until 4 days after the rash appears (Recall)

