## Question 10

A 44 years old woman presents to the ED with pain in his right eye, after initial assessment you suspect corneal ulcer. Regarding sensory innervation, which one of the following nerves carry pain sensation from cornea?

- A. Facial nerve
- B. Maxillary division of trigeminal nerve
- **C. Opthalmic division of trigeminal nerve** (Correct Answer)
- D. Mandibular division of trigeminal nerve
- E. Optic nerve

**Correct Answer:** C

