- **E. Right abducent nerve** (Correct Answer)

**Correct Answer:** E

**Explanation:**

Paralysis of right lateral rectus muscle (LR-6) resulted due to palsy of 6th cranial nerve. Patient will be unable to abduct the eye and will result in t he affected eye being unable to turn outwards.

