The shoulder Joint (High Yield)

Type: synovial ball and socket joint

Shoulder joint is formed by the articulation of th e head of the humerus with the glenoid cavity o f the scapula

Ligaments of the shoulder joint:

In the shoulder joint, the ligaments play a key role in stabilizing the bony structures.

